Lolly patch 0004: the project library lives in Lolly.

Why: an opaque-origin frame has no IndexedDB, so openIdb() serves the store
the utility hands over (kept in host.state by the utility, through the
frame's postMessage protocol). The library also opens the utility's own song
(its code, language and name inputs) the way it files a share link, and
reports every edit, project switch, rename and language toggle back, so the
utility's inputs, Save and share links always hold the song. A song changed
on the utility's side (undo, a collaborator) goes into the open project.

Applied by scripts/vendor-rondocode.ts with git apply --directory=packages/rondo/upstream.

